          ],
          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "Pad every gamepad binding in this map reads from. Defaults to the primary pad (slot 0). This is RUNTIME context, not part of a binding: an action still binds the semantic control (GamepadButton.South), and the map rebases it onto this pad's slot. Nothing about the pad is ever serialized, so a two-player save file describes one control scheme rather than two slot-specific ones. Local multiplayer is therefore one map per player: ts const p1 = new ActionMap({ ... }, { gamepad: this.inputs.gamepads[0] }); const p2 = new ActionMap({ ... }, { gamepad: this.inputs.gamepads[1] });  A Gamepad is a stable slot mailbox that outlives any physical device, so a map keeps working across disconnect and reconnect."
        }
      ],
